## What the previous review found (the author's summary of it — verify, do not 
trust)

| Id | Finding | Claimed correction |
|---|---|---|
| R1 | G2 FAIL: the Project Browser still filtered levels by 
`ElementId(10)/(11)`, `level_view_name` did not resolve `View::Level(id)`, and 
`sheet_draw`/`view3d` selected level 10 | Browser adds the levels after the 
tree's own two, by position; search matches the shown name; `level_view_name` 
resolves `View::Level`; `sheet_draw::plan_level_id` resolves plan keys from the
document; the 3D drop falls back to the document's lowest level; `view_ui` 
documents `p10`/`p11` as view names, with the key scheme deliberately unchanged
(it would invalidate stored view settings and sheet references) |
| R2 | G3 FAIL: `tool_has_pending_points` omitted `edit_ref`, `opening_host`, 
`view_corner`, `view_edit`; Beam, Truss and a one-point Duct/Pipe run left the 
tool on the first Esc | All four states added; Beam, Truss and the one-point 
run step back first; tested for each |
| R3 | G5 FAIL: Beam, Column, Truss and the footing commands still inherited 
shared numbers | The framing tools and both footing commands start from their 
own numbers; the Foundation button initialises everything an isolated pad 
consumes |
| R4 | G6 FAIL: the rename field rebuilt its draft every frame, so typing was 
lost | The draft lives in the app 
(`start_level_rename`/`commit_level_rename`/`cancel_level_rename`); the field 
stays open on a refused name; tested over frames |
| R5 | G8 FAIL: `clipboard_events` moved in the input order, and the office 
test did not exercise the whole window | Clipboard keys keep their original 
place; the journey chooses every tool by clicking its ribbon button, aims its 
pointer clicks with the plan's own transform, and compares every element's 
identity, geometry and name plus the room's area on reopen |
| R6 | G10 FAIL: four backlog rows had acceptance that depended on another 
row's deliverable, two in a cycle | IFC-001 no longer requires IFC-002; MEP-002
is hydraulic/airflow only and MEP-005 owns the electrical import without 
depending on SCH-004 (P2); SCH-004 depends on MEP-005; TEST-001 is the harness 
and the office (P0) and the data-hall chain is the new MEP-004 (P3) |

The previous review also recorded G11 FAIL (the desktop suite had one failing 
